events:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset: spr-valentus-cloak-events, genuine chunky pixel RPG sprite sheet, actual transparent alpha PNG. Exactly FOUR columns and THREE rows, TWELVE isolated sprites, equal square cells, 4:3 canvas preferably 1536 x 1152, no labels, no grid lines.
Character is exactly the same hooded injured Valentus from the last generated run sheet. Attached films establish his identity: lean serious adult, dark long center-parted hair as a few strands under his low hood, small short chin beard, no full beard. Thick dark tattered hooded wool cloak pulled over eyes, midnight navy #172535 / black-green #182A23, dark blue robe #1F3550 underneath with small ivory edge #E8E2D0, heavy dark leather metal-studded pointed beak-toe boots. Cloth cloak, NO armor. Dark blood #9A3438 on anatomical RIGHT side below ribs. His RIGHT hand guards the wound except when both hands are required for climbing. This is the desperate injured escape through moonlit woods from the prologue, increasingly exhausted, never acrobatic or triumphant.
STYLE matches attached pixel-RPG reference and last run sheet: uniform big square pixel clusters, adult realistic 6-7 head height proportions, hard dark stepped outline, sparse flat discrete colors, 3 tones per material, cold moon-silver #B8C4D6 edge accents. Each pose made at approximately 48 x 64 logical pixels then enlarged with nearest neighbor. No phototextures, smooth gradients, glow, blur, soft anti-aliasing, intricate texture, chibi, text, UI.
All poses face EAST, SCREEN RIGHT. Fixed slightly elevated 3/4 RPG camera. Same character body scale in every cell even when lying horizontal. Clear generous transparent margins. No environment or ground sprites: the root, brook, ledge, tree and slippery stone are provided separately by the game. Convey contact with those INVISIBLE obstacles through precise body gestures. No water or tree objects, no ground shadows.
ROW 1, four chronological phases of STUMBLING OVER A LARGE ROOT:
c1 eastward stooped running step with forward RIGHT boot abruptly caught, torso beginning to tip, right hand tight to wound;
c2 pitching sharply forward, rear leg kicked upward and left arm shooting forward;
c3 near falling, left hand reaching low to arrest fall, knees bent and cloak thrown over back;
c4 regaining his feet hunched, braced left leg forward and right hand gripping flank.
ROW 2, BROOK JUMP AND EXHAUSTION:
c1 takeoff: deep crouch on rear left leg, pushing forward east, right hand holding wound;
c2 flight: clearly airborne eastward, both knees tucked, cloak streaming behind to left; keep aerial feet higher within cell;
c3 landing: forward right boot meets common ground baseline, left knee buckles, torso folds forward, left arm balancing;
c4 panting recovery: standing hunched deeply over wounded RIGHT side, right hand pressed under ribs, mouth open gasping.
ROW 3, FOUR DISTINCT ROMAN ESCAPE LANDMARKS:
c1 pulling himself over a high ledge on right: both arms reaching high east, fingers hooked over invisible lip, chest to edge, one knee raised against ledge, boots trailing below;
c2 bracing against a crooked tree on right: LEFT palm at head height on invisible tree, weight leaning into extended arm, right hand still on wound, bent knees;
c3 slipping on wet stone: feet slide FORWARD toward right, hips low, torso thrown back to left, left arm flails, right hand on wound;
c4 lying collapsed on his side on ground: body horizontal, hooded head towards RIGHT, boots at LEFT, knees slightly bent, right forearm gripping injured flank, clearly no standing stance.
Preserve exact 4x3 regular grid, exactly one full-body pose per cell, no cropping, no overlap, exact consistent adult limb scale, common ground baseline in grounded cells; aerial and climbing pose have deliberate action offsets only. Whole isolated sprite sheet on transparent canvas. No staff, weapons, armor, magic effects, runes, banners, emblems, castles, monsters, neon.
